---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy Policy — Contractor License Lookup"
  description="How contractorlicenselookup.org handles visitor data."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p>Last updated: November 4, 2026.</p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>
      Contractor License Lookup doesn’t ask you to sign up or give us any personal information. We use Google
      Analytics to count visits and see which pages and features people use, so we know what to improve.
    </p>

    <h2 id="analytics">Google Analytics</h2>
    <ul class="points">
      <li>
        Google Analytics sets cookies (<code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_JD3MX1WLKC</code>) and sends Google which pages
        you view, roughly where you are, your device and browser type, and the site that sent you here.
      </li>
      <li>
        On the California search we count how many searches are made, whether they found anything and how often
        details are opened. We never send what you searched for: no names, words or license numbers.
      </li>
      <li>No advertising features, Google signals or ad personalization are turned on.</li>
      <li>
        If your browser is set to a European time zone, Google Analytics stays off unless you accept it in the banner.
        Google also treats visitors it locates in the EEA, the UK and Switzerland as not having consented.
      </li>
      <li>
        We honor Global Privacy Control: if your browser sends it, Google Analytics doesn’t run. Automated browsers
        aren’t counted either.
      </li>
      <li>
        Google processes this data under its own terms. See
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener">how Google
        uses information from sites that use its services</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <div class="choices" id="choices">
      <p data-choice-status>Your analytics choice is stored in this browser only.</p>
      <button class="button secondary" type="button" data-set="denied">Turn analytics off</button>
      <button class="button secondary" type="button" data-set="granted" hidden>Turn analytics on</button>
    </div>
    <script is:inline>
      (function () {
        var a = window.cllAnalytics;
        var box = document.getElementById('choices');
        if (!a || !box) return;
        var status = box.querySelector('[data-choice-status]');
        var off = box.querySelector('[data-set="denied"]');
        var on = box.querySelector('[data-set="granted"]');
        function render() {
          var running = a.enabled();
          if (a.gpc) status.textContent = 'Your browser sends Global Privacy Control, so Google Analytics is off.';
          else status.textContent = running ? 'Google Analytics is on in this browser.' : 'Google Analytics is off in this browser.';
          off.hidden = !running || a.gpc;
          on.hidden = running || a.gpc;
        }
        box.addEventListener('click', function (event) {
          var value = event.target && event.target.getAttribute && event.target.getAttribute('data-set');
          if (!value) return;
          a.set(value);
          if (value === 'denied') location.reload();
          else render();
        });
        render();
      })();
    </script>

    <h2>The California license search</h2>
    <p>
      The search runs in your browser on a copy of the Contractors State License Board’s public license file. What
      you type isn’t sent to us: your browser only downloads the part of the list it needs, named after the first
      three letters of a word or the range of license numbers. The search is kept in the page address after a
      <code>#</code>, which browsers don’t send to websites.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      The site is hosted on Cloudflare. Like any web host, Cloudflare processes technical data such as IP addresses to
      deliver pages and protect the site from abuse. See
      <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Cloudflare’s privacy policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Links to official boards</h2>
    <p>
      We link to official state board websites so you can confirm a license there. Those sites have their own privacy
      policies.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If we add advertising or change what we collect, we will update this page first and explain how to opt out.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about privacy: <a href="mailto:contact@contractorlicenselookup.org">contact@contractorlicenselookup.org</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
